ASoC: xilinx: formatter_pcm: pass aud_drv_data as IRQ cookie in configure_{mm2s,s2mm}()

Stable commit 0d58a70b6dc7b ("ASoC: xilinx: formatter_pcm: pass aud_drv_data to
irq handlers") changes xlnx_mm2s_irq_handler()/xlnx_s2mm_irq_handler() to take
the struct xlnx_pcm_drv_data as dev_id, and passes aud_drv_data to
devm_request_irq() in xlnx_formatter_pcm_probe(). Downstream main moved the IRQ
requests into configure_mm2s() and configure_s2mm() and the probe conflicts were
resolved to call those helpers, so the cookie change was lost: the handlers
(merged without conflict) would treat the struct device as xlnx_pcm_drv_data.

Pass aud_drv_data in the downstream helpers as well.

diff --git a/sound/soc/xilinx/xlnx_formatter_pcm.c b/sound/soc/xilinx/xlnx_formatter_pcm.c
--- a/sound/soc/xilinx/xlnx_formatter_pcm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/xilinx/xlnx_formatter_pcm.c
@@ -673,7 +673,7 @@
 
 	ret = devm_request_irq(dev, aud_drv_data->mm2s_irq,
 			       xlnx_mm2s_irq_handler, 0,
-			       "xlnx_formatter_pcm_mm2s_irq", dev);
+			       "xlnx_formatter_pcm_mm2s_irq", aud_drv_data);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "xlnx audio mm2s irq request failed\n");
 		return ret;
@@ -723,7 +723,7 @@
 	ret = devm_request_irq(dev, aud_drv_data->s2mm_irq,
 			       xlnx_s2mm_irq_handler, 0,
 			       "xlnx_formatter_pcm_s2mm_irq",
-			       dev);
+			       aud_drv_data);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "xlnx audio s2mm irq request failed\n");
 		return ret;
